    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Bug Type: Visual / Animation (possible hitbox mismatch)<br/>
Priority: Low</p>

<p>Preconditions:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running and the player is in a combat room that contains a spike trap.</li>
	<li><span class="error">&#91;Nhân vật dùng khi test, ví dụ Pyrois&#93;</span>.</li>
</ul>


<p>Steps to Reproduce:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Enter a combat room with a spike trap.</li>
	<li>Step onto the outer edge of the spike row.</li>
	<li>Stay there while the trap turns red (0.5s) and the spikes pop up.</li>
	<li>Observe the character and the HP/armor on the HUD.</li>
</ol>


<p>Expected Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The trap warns in red for 0.5s, then the spikes pop up (TC-SP-01).</li>
	<li>A player still standing on the trap takes 1 damage (armor first, then HP) (TC-SP-02).</li>
	<li>What the player sees on screen matches where damage is applied.</li>
</ul>


<p>Actual Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>The character appears to walk into the spike row, but only reaches its outer edge.</li>
	<li>The player takes no damage when the spikes pop up.</li>
	<li>HUD armor and HP stay unchanged.</li>
</ul>


<p>Test Case Result:</p>

<ul>
	<li>FAIL</li>
	<li>Related Test Cases: TC-SP-02 (trap damages a player who stays on it), TC-SP-01 (red warning 0.5s before the spikes pop up)</li>
</ul>


<p>Notes:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Likely the spike sprite or animation is larger than the damage area, so the character looks like it is inside the trap while the hitbox is not.</li>
	<li>Verify whether this is only visual or whether the damage area really does not cover the edge. Check the trap’s collision shape against its sprite.</li>
	<li>Check whether this happens on all sides of the trap and with all characters.</li>
	<li>Check whether I-Frames are active at that moment (TC-SP-06), to rule out a false positive.</li>
	<li>Attach a screen recording.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
